<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>3.3.1.5 Task: Degree of product of quadratics</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p class="tb-exercise">Exercise</p>
<p>Two polynomials are</p>
<p>\[ f(x) = {@p@} \quad \text{and} \quad g(x) = {@q@}. \]</p>
<p>Without expanding the product, write down the degree of the product \(f(x)\,g(x)\).</p>
<div>Degree of \(f(x)\,g(x)\) = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The <strong>degree</strong> of a polynomial is the highest power of \(x\) with a non-zero coefficient. When two polynomials are multiplied, the highest-power term of the product comes only from multiplying the two leading terms, and powers of \(x\) <strong>add</strong> when terms are multiplied: \(x^m \times x^n = x^{m+n}\). Because neither leading coefficient is zero, their product is not zero either. So the degree of a product is the <strong>sum</strong> of the degrees, not their product.</p>
<p>Here \(f(x)\) has leading term \({@lt1@}\), so it has degree \({@m@}\), and \(g(x)\) has leading term \({@lt2@}\), so it has degree \({@n@}\). The leading term of \(f(x)\,g(x)\) is</p>
<p>\[ \left({@lt1@}\right)\left({@lt2@}\right) = {@lt1*lt2@}, \]</p>
<p>so the product has degree \({@m@} + {@n@} = {@ta1@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[/* Degree m times degree n. The pair (2,2) is excluded because 2+2 = 2*2, which would let
   "multiplied the degrees" score. n starts at 2 so that m*n never equals max(m,n): the
   two diagnostics (m*n and "kept the larger degree") stay distinct on every seed.
   ta1-1 (wrong test) never equals m*n or max(m,n) for these pairs. */
pr: rand([[2,3],[2,4],[3,2],[3,3],[3,4],[4,2],[4,3],[4,4]]);
m: first(pr);
n: second(pr);
a1: rand_with_prohib(-5, 5, [0]);
b1: rand_with_prohib(-6, 6, [0]);
c1: rand_with_prohib(-9, 9, [0]);
a2: rand_with_prohib(-5, 5, [0]);
b2: rand_with_prohib(-6, 6, [0]);
c2: rand_with_prohib(-9, 9, [0]);
p: a1*x^m + b1*x + c1;
q: a2*x^n + b2*x^(n-1) + c2;
lt1: a1*x^m;
lt2: a2*x^n;
ta1: hipow(expand(p*q), x);
wrong_mult: m*n;
wrong_max: max(m, n);]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
